docs/product/search-notes.md:1:# Search — product notes
docs/product/search-notes.md:3:_Written for the search dialog launch (2025-11). Kept for history; see `docs/adr/0007-search-query-language.md` for the current rules._
docs/product/search-notes.md:5:## What search does
docs/product/search-notes.md:7:Search is a substring match over issue titles and descriptions, comment bodies and project
docs/product/search-notes.md:8:names. Results are newest-indexed first. It is deliberately not a search engine.
docs/product/search-notes.md:10:## Advanced search (Enterprise)
docs/product/search-notes.md:12:Advanced search adds the query prefixes `kind:` (alias `in:`) and `project:`. The dialog shows a
docs/product/search-notes.md:13:hint line ("searching comments · in project …") so people see what we understood before they
docs/product/search-notes.md:17:search we show "Field-scoped search is not included in this plan" rather than silently searching
docs/product/search-notes.md:26:project-scoped search returns issues only; the comment results come back when the project
docs/product/search-notes.md:31:The palette asks for issues only unless Advanced search is on, in which case it asks for
docs/product/search-notes.md:32:issues, comments and projects. The search page always asks for what the person ticked.
docs/adr/0007-search-query-language.md:1:# ADR 0007 — The search query language
docs/adr/0007-search-query-language.md:5:- Supersedes: the "Search" section of `docs/product/search-notes.md` where the two disagree.
docs/adr/0007-search-query-language.md:9:Workspace search is a substring index (`search_index`) maintained on every write and queried by
docs/adr/0007-search-query-language.md:10:the command palette, the search page and the search API. The dialog grew a small query language
docs/adr/0007-search-query-language.md:20:2. **Field tokens exist only for workspaces that have `advanced_search`.** A token is a word of the
docs/adr/0007-search-query-language.md:24:     present it decides which kinds are searched, whatever the caller's `kinds` said.
docs/adr/0007-search-query-language.md:31:3. **Without `advanced_search` the whole query is free text.** A colon is just a character
docs/adr/0007-search-query-language.md:34:4. **Without `advanced_search` only issues are searched.** Whatever kinds the caller asks for,
docs/adr/0007-search-query-language.md:36:   `kind:` tokens, rule 2) are honoured. `advanced_search` is evaluated like every other flag:
docs/adr/0007-search-query-language.md:40:   so what the dialog says it understood is what the server searches.
docs/adr/0007-search-query-language.md:42:6. **Comments belong to their issue's project in the index.** A comment's search document carries
docs/adr/0007-search-query-language.md:45:   on creation, on edit, on a rebuild of the workspace index, and on a reindex request.
docs/adr/0007-search-query-language.md:47:7. **Reindex requests cover every kind.** A `search.reindex_requested` event for an issue, a
docs/adr/0007-search-query-language.md:55:- Searching `Release 2: hotfix` on a Starter workspace finds the issue with that title.
